{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/699941-how-to-use-gwnet","id":699941,"title":"How to use GWNet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-13T10:51:27-07:00","id":699941,"title":"How to use GWNet","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I want to introduce the GWNet in my games, but I also would like not to spoil the reach of the information and help the players can get from it. If it connects all Glass Walkers, the probability of someone being able to find information is very high - something that makes allies and contacts backgrounds a little bit redundant.<br /> <br /> How do you work with it? Is it tied to any background (Tribe prestige, Contacts, allies)?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5426-aecioborba","name":"aecioborba","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T16:24:24-07:00","id":700237,"title":"","content":"How useful GWNet is depends on what you search. It's going to have lots of information about bigger threats, but every piece of information has to come from somewhere and not every GW will bother to type up all their knowledge. And if you ask for something, someone else has to take time out of their schedule to answer you or perhaps even do research for you. People who care enough about you to do that are called Contacts.<br /> In general, I've found that regular Contacts and GWNet fill different niches: GWNet is for the bigger picture, Contacts make sure you know what's going on around you, in your city which may have maybe ten other Glasswalkers if you're lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:06:46-07:00","id":700726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/699941-how-to-use-gwnet?p=700237#post700237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How useful GWNet is depends on what you search. It's going to have lots of information about bigger threats, but every piece of information has to come from somewhere and not every GW will bother to type up all their knowledge. And if you ask for something, someone else has to take time out of their schedule to answer you or perhaps even do research for you. People who care enough about you to do that are called Contacts.<br /> In general, I've found that regular Contacts and GWNet fill different niches: GWNet is for the bigger picture, Contacts make sure you know what's going on around you, in your city which may have maybe ten other Glasswalkers if you're lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>And remember that the BSDs can probably see everything on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:33:14-07:00","id":700753,"title":"","content":"I don't see why they would be able to do that. While not much is written about what the Net actually is, I'd consider it reasonably safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T09:18:10-07:00","id":700957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/699941-how-to-use-gwnet?p=700753#post700753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they would be able to do that. While not much is written about what the Net actually is, I'd consider it reasonably safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>BSD's have traitors and infiltrators among the Garou, It's safe to assume they have access to GW.net.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T00:57:31-07:00","id":704451,"title":"","content":"GW.NET could be a massive awakened machine that has the power to make itself inaccessible by those with Wyrm taint, or those who aren't children of Cockroach, I suppose.<br /> If that were the case, then it could nye impossible for a Wyrm creature to access it.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say that the Weaver couldn't hack it, or that a foolish GW might not have his own computer's security, or local security tight enough and something could monitor what comes through his monitor, or private Email/messenger accounts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T03:11:03-07:00","id":704614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/699941-how-to-use-gwnet?p=704451#post704451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GW.NET could be a massive awakened machine that has the power to make itself inaccessible by those with Wyrm taint, or those who aren't children of Cockroach, I suppose.<br /> If that were the case, then it could nye impossible for a Wyrm creature to access it.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say that the Weaver couldn't hack it, or that a foolish GW might not have his own computer's security, or local security tight enough and something could monitor what comes through his monitor, or private Email/messenger accounts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh come on, that's a copout :P Those spirits could be easily tricked by all the infiltration BSD gifts. You should treat the GW.Net as an actual network. It's going to have cliques, levels, organizations and circles of trust. Just because it's something everyone can use doesn't mean everyone has access to everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}